<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- UMW_Melee. BodyColor + Appearance + Eltex. The body is plated in eltex, Royalty's psychically
       resonant alloy, the way every Royalty eltex garment is. First of the eltex trio (with
       UMW_EltexFitted and UMW_LeadLined, both in this folder), which splits the four weapon-routed
       psychic stats by canon: Plated mirrors the eltex garments (sensitivity offset plus neural heat
       recovery), Fitted mirrors Anomaly's bioferrite stuff (sensitivity factor plus heat limit).
       INTENT: "a fighting weapon that does part of an eltex garment's job."
       Routing: Core's PsychicSensitivity and PsychicEntropyRecoveryRate carry StatPart_GearStatOffset
       with includeWeapon, which reads the primary weapon's PsychicSensitivityOffset /
       PsychicEntropyRecoveryRateOffset as a weapon-thing stat, so CompUniqueWeapon.GetStatOffset
       hands it this trait's statOffsets and the pawn's breakdown lists the weapon under "Relevant
       gear". No hediff, no patch, no TraitEffectSummary case: vanilla renders the lines on the trait
       card. The new weapon-stat caches are cleared on landing by
       Patches/CompUniqueWeapon_TraitStatCache_Patch.cs, as for every trait-named stat.
       Scaling: the sensitivity offset is QUALITY-SCALED by the stat's own StatPart_Quality (as eltex
       apparel is), so 0.20 is the Good value: 0.10 Awful, 0.30 Legendary. The recovery offset has no
       quality part and is flat. The quality-less VFEP warcasket pair reads as Normal (x0.83, so
       +0.166), accepted.
       Anchors: sensitivity at the eltex robe's +0.20; recovery between the eltex vest's +0.033 and
       the helmet's +0.066; MarketValue +120 at the Monomolecular premium tier (added capability is an
       offset). A legendary Plated + Fitted weapon lands at about +0.43 equivalent sensitivity, under
       the eltex staff's +0.50, so a weapon that also fights never out-focuses the focus item.
       Double-edged by construction: sensitivity raises exposure to psychic drones, shock and insanity
       lances and soothe/insanity events, which is why the eltex pair needs no malus.
       Tokens: BodyColor (it forces UMW_EltexPale onto colour two via ForcedColorTwoExtension, so it
       replaces the stuff tint and excludes the other body finishes), Appearance (as the body finishes
       carry it), and Eltex so a plated weapon is never also lead-lined. Fitted sits on the accent
       channel and deliberately lacks Eltex, so the two co-roll: the full-set reward.
       Root: eltex is Royalty canon and every vanilla eltex item is techLevel Ultra, so the def lives
       in the Royalty compat root (the folder is the gate, no MayRequire) and the war merchant's
       scoped ultratech ban in Patches/CompUniqueWeapon_DisabledTraits_Patch.cs names it. Vanilla
       Psycasts Expanded's medieval eltex weapons are VPE's canon, not followed; nothing here needs
       VPE. canGenerateAlone true, a real effect like the Royalty trio; commonality 0.35 rather than the
       trio's 0.5 because the eltex pair is two traits (Fitted's header). -->
  <WeaponTraitDef>
    <defName>UMW_EltexPlated</defName>
    <label>eltex-plated</label>
    <description>The body is plated in eltex, a psychically resonant alloy, under a pale sheen. It sharpens the wielder's psychic sensitivity and bleeds away neural heat.</description>
    <commonality>0.35</commonality>
    <weaponCategory>UMW_Melee</weaponCategory>
    <exclusionTags>
      <li>BodyColor</li>
      <li>Appearance</li>
      <li>Eltex</li>
    </exclusionTags>
    <statOffsets>
      <PsychicSensitivityOffset>0.20</PsychicSensitivityOffset> <!-- Good-quality value; quality-scaled by the stat's own part -->
      <PsychicEntropyRecoveryRateOffset>0.05</PsychicEntropyRecoveryRateOffset> <!-- not quality-scaled -->
      <MarketValue>120</MarketValue> <!-- premium tier, cf. Monomolecular +120 -->
    </statOffsets>
    <traitAdjectives>
      <li>eltex-plated</li>
      <li>pale-sheened</li>
      <li>resonant</li>
    </traitAdjectives>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="UniqueMeleeWeapons.ForcedColorTwoExtension">
        <color>UMW_EltexPale</color>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </WeaponTraitDef>

</Defs>
